मण्डलम् पदविभाग ॥

॰ ADR-0030 REMEDIATION, TASK `D-002h`. THE FILE TAKEN BY THIS CYCLE IS THIS ONE,
॰ THE FIFTH OF THE REPAIR after `ir.t1`, `ast.t1`, `vishlesana.t1` and
॰ `artha.t1`. All 74 of its 64-bit integer positions read `अ६४` and now read
॰ `न६४`, and not one moves the other way: this file holds NO signed quantity.
॰ Every site is a भेद numbered from १, a BYTE OFFSET into मूल, a LENGTH, an
॰ AKṢARA (code-point) INDEX, a 1-based LINE, or the arena's write index — and
॰ none of the six can be negative. The file moves by exactly what the census
॰ sees: it wraps no 64-bit type in `अङ्कः अन्तः`, `सम्भाव्य` or `दोषयुक्त`,
॰ so this is the first file since `ir.t1` whose count and whose ledger agree.
॰
॰ THE TWIN IS `crates/sadhana/src/lex.rs` AND IT HAS NO `i64` AND NO `isize`
॰ AT ALL. `Token::{byte, aksara, line}` and `LexError::{byte, index, line}`
॰ are every numeric field the module declares and all six are `usize`; `Kind`
॰ and `Karaka` are enums. `t1_sources.rs`'s `T0_LEXER_KINDS` already pairs the
॰ eight `*भेद` above with their `lex.rs` variant, so the reading is not made
॰ here for the first time — it is READ OFF A MAPPING THE GATE ALREADY HOLDS.
॰
॰ AND THIS IS THE FIRST FILE WHOSE CASE FOR UNSIGNED IS MADE BY THE CODE AND
॰ NOT ONLY BY THE TWIN. `artha.t1` argued from a twin that declared every sign;
॰ `ast.t1` had a twin that ran out. Here the argument is also INTERNAL, and it
॰ is the two shapes a signed reading would need and this file does not have:
॰   · EVERY SUBTRACTION IS GUARDED. `टिप्पणीसीमा`'s `सीमा वियोगः २` stands
॰     under a `यदि सीमा न्यूनम् ३` that returns first; `पुच्छविरामः`'s
॰     `सीमा वियोगः ६` and `सीमा वियोगः ३` under `दैर्घ्य अधिकम् ६` and
॰     `अधिकम् ३`; `विभज`'s three `सीमा वियोगः १`/`२`/`३` under
॰     `दैर्घ्य न्यूनम् ३`. The `सीमा वियोगः आरम्भः` in `विरामचिह्न`,
॰     `पुच्छविरामः` and `विभज` rests on आरम्भः ≤ सीमा, the range contract
॰     every caller in `पदविभाग` keeps. No difference here can go below ०.
॰   · THERE IS NO NEGATIVE SENTINEL. `विरामचिह्न` and `विभज` answer ० for
॰     "not a sign" and "no kāraka" — the comment at `विरामचिह्न` says so and
॰     cites वाक्यविभाग's कारक for the same choice — and `पदादिः`,
॰     `पदान्तिकम्` and `पुच्छविरामः` answer सीमा for "not found". A port that
॰     had reached for −१ would be the one place a signed type was earned, and
॰     this one did not.
॰ Both are properties a file-wide `sed` cannot check and a reader can, which is
॰ why the pass still goes site by site.

॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
॰ THE T0 LEXER — a port of crates/sadhana/src/lex.rs `lex`.
॰
॰ Devanagari source in, चिह्नक out. The atom is the akṣara and every
॰ offset reported is a character index as well as a byte offset, which is
॰ the one thing the previous state of this file DID get right.
॰
॰ ── WHAT THIS FILE WAS, AND WHY THE ROW EXISTS (D-002f10) ──
॰ Until this commit चिह्नककोश appeared EXACTLY ONCE in this file — its
॰ declaration below — and was never written to. पदविभाग walked the source
॰ counting akṣaras and returned ०; विरामचिह्न returned ० for every input.
॰ Only विभज was real, and विभज could not be CALLED, for the reason in the
॰ next paragraph. So D-002f3/f4/f6 would each have read an empty arena and
॰ every test of them would have had to hand-build tokens.
॰
॰ ── THE REASON IT WAS EMPTY, WHICH IS A LANGUAGE FACT AND NOT AN OVERSIGHT ──
॰ T1 HAS NO SLICE CONSTRUCTOR AND NO ITERATOR. There is no way in this
॰ language to write `&source[a..b]`. Every routine here whose signature
॰ said `शब्द ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८` was therefore UNCALLABLE from a lexer that
॰ has only the whole source and two offsets, and every routine whose
॰ return type was `अङ्कः अन्तः चिह्नक` could only ever answer ०. A body
॰ that cannot be written is written as `प्रत्यागमनम् ०`, and that is
॰ exactly what was here.
॰
॰ सङ्केतन met the same wall and settled it: its row readers take
॰ (पाठ्यम् ऽ आरम्भः ऽ सीमा) — the whole text and a HALF-OPEN BYTE RANGE —
॰ and it says so out loud at अष्टकान्वेषणम्, *"the whole of Rust's `split`
॰ and `split_once`, T1 having no iterator to return"*. This file adopts
॰ that convention rather than inventing a second one. Concretely:
॰
॰   · विरामचिह्न and विभज are re-signed from (शब्द) to (मूल ऽ आरम्भः ऽ सीमा).
॰     Their arithmetic is UNCHANGED — विभज already indexed from the end,
॰     so दैर्घ्य became सीमा वियोगः आरम्भः and शब्द अङ्कः दैर्घ्य वियोगः १ अन्तः
॰     became मूल अङ्कः सीमा वियोगः १ अन्तः. No sigil table is restated.
॰     THIS IS THE CHANGE THAT MAKES विभज CALLABLE FOR THE FIRST TIME.
॰   · चिह्नक keeps every field व्याक्यविभाग names — भेद, पाठ, अष्टक, अक्षर,
॰     पङ्क्ति — and GAINS ONE, पाठसीमा. पाठ is the text the token lies IN
॰     (the whole source), अष्टक is where the token starts and पाठसीमा is
॰     where it ends. That is सङ्केतन's triple stored in a record. The token
॰     shape is EXTENDED and not altered: no field lost a name or a type, so
॰     वाक्यविभाग's note on this record is still true as written.
॰   · पदविभाग returns न६४ — how many tokens it wrote — and not
॰     `दोषयुक्त अङ्कः अन्तः चिह्नक`. The arena is module state under the
॰     preallocated कोश + सूचकाङ्क convention that व्याकर, मध्यरूप and
॰     वाक्यविभाग all adopted, and every appender in those files returns the
॰     index for the same reason. A return type this language cannot build
॰     is how `प्रत्यागमनम् ०` got written the first time.
॰
॰ ── WHAT IS PORTED AND WHAT IS NOT ──
॰ Ported: lex.rs's line walk, its akṣara bookkeeping, `pieces`'s comment
॰ strip (lex.rs:295's `line.split('॰').next()`), `split_whitespace`,
॰ `split_trailing_punct`, `punctuation`, and `split_sigil` (विभज).
॰
॰ NOT ported, each blocked on a named thing that does not exist:
॰   (a) repertoire::check — `sanskrit_text::repertoire` is a DERIVED TABLE
॰       and no .t1 module holds it. This is the same blocker सङ्केतन's four
॰       table readers are pinned on. So this port CANNOT FAIL, which is why
॰       the दोष record below is declared and has no arena: an arena nothing
॰       can write is the defect this row exists to remove, and adding one
॰       here would have reproduced it one level down.
॰   (b) is_numeral — CORRECTED 2026-09-01, and the correction is the whole
॰       point of auditing a blocker before believing it. This read
॰       "अक्षरकोश ॱ सङ्ख्या is a stub". IT IS NOT, and had not been for some
॰       time: sanskrit_text.t1:21 reads the base, validates the digits and
॰       accumulates the value. THE THIRD CLAIM IS FALSE AND THE ROUTINE IS
॰       RIGHT — corrected again 2026-09-05, after a change made on the strength
॰       of this sentence had to be reverted. `सङ्ख्या` IS THE RADIX READER: it
॰       reads the base, validates every digit and ANSWERS THE BASE, and
॰       `t1_execution.rs`'s corpus agreement pins it against Rust's `radix`.
॰       The file's VALUE reader is `मानम्` beside `मानदोषः`, and its BIT reader
॰       is `अंशाः` beside `अंशदोषः` — three readers that answer differently, which
॰       is the point of the test named for it. A margin that credits a mechanism
॰       nobody has run is worth less than no margin: this one said "accumulates
॰       the value" of a routine that does not and must not, and cost a red main.
॰       सङ्ख्याभेद is STILL never produced here, but
॰       BY DESIGN and not for want of a routine — see (d): T0 वाक्यविभाग
॰       requires an operand to arrive as पदभेद. One lexer serves T0 and T1,
॰       so व्याकर decides numeral-ness by TEXT (parse.t1, अभिव्यञ्जकपठनम्)
॰       rather than have this file take a side that would break T0.
॰   (c) TRUE akṣara segmentation — अक्षरकोश ॱ अक्षराणि is a stub too, so
॰       अक्षरगणना counts CODE POINTS by UTF-8 lead byte, which is what this
॰       file always counted. क्ष is three code points and one akṣara, so the
॰       अक्षर field is a code-point index until that stub lands. Recorded
॰       here because the old file's count looked correct and was not.
॰   (d) Kind::Operand — T1 HAS NO OPERAND KIND, by वाक्यविभाग's design:
॰       an operand lexes as पदभेद and the reader calls विभज for the role
॰       and takes the base by length. So this lexer does not call विभज at
॰       all, and that is the landed shape and not an omission.
॰   (e) Kind::Str and ADR-0018's layout words belong to `lex_t1`, the T1
॰       entry point, and not to `lex`. Different row.
॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

॰ `आयातः वास्तु ।` STOOD HERE UNTIL 2026-09-04 (W-225) and was REMOVED: this
॰ file names no `वास्तुॱ…` anywhere — the lexer produces tokens, not AST — so
॰ the import reached nothing. `lex.rs` likewise uses nothing from `ast.rs`.

सार्वजनिक चरः पदभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।   ॰ Kind::Word — and Kind::Operand, which folds here
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्ख्याभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।   ॰ Kind::Numeral
सार्वजनिक चरः शब्दभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।   ॰ Kind::Str
सार्वजनिक चरः दण्डभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ४ ।   ॰ Kind::Danda
सार्वजनिक चरः युग्मदण्डभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ५ ।   ॰ Kind::DoubleDanda
